---
# yamllint disable rule:line-length
# The object-mapper half of the `count()` guard (#973, #635). `142` keeps a
# count-preserving stage native by stamping the Φ.hone.lambda `111` lifted out
# of it; a `.map(new Foo())` never becomes a lambda, so `142` walks past it and
# the elision `101` and `142` were written to protect is lost again the moment
# `215` starts lifting object mappers.
#
# The defect is `101`'s, verbatim. A `count()` that `101` did NOT stamp is one
# the JVM can elide: the source is SIZED, `map` preserves SIZED, and
# `ReferencePipeline.count()` answers from the spliterator without running the
# pipeline at all. `Stream.of(1, 2, 3).map(new Loud()).count()` therefore calls
# `Loud.apply` zero times today; fuse the map into a `mapMulti`, which clears
# SIZED by design, and it is called once per element. Same specification, more
# work, and the fusion it buys optimises a pipeline that was never going to run.
#
# So this rule stamps the `invokeinterface Stream.map` itself with
# `reverted ↦ Φ.true`. `215` is closed on the four-binding opcode jeo emits, so
# a stamped one stops matching it, never becomes a Φ.hone.named-map, never folds
# into a distill, and the `new`/`dup`/`invokespecial` in front of it are left
# exactly where javac put them. jeo ignores the extra binding when assembling,
# the same way it ignores the one `441` leaves on a reverted `distinct`.
#
# Only the map needs it. A `filter(new Bar())` clears SIZED whatever its
# argument is, so `101` stamps the terminal, `142` and this rule both stand
# down, and the object filter fuses as it should.
#
# Like `142` this is closed on the unstamped opcode, so it cannot re-fire on its
# own output, and it runs after `102` has taken the own-line label out from
# between the constructor and the call, which is what makes the constructor run
# and the stream call adjacent enough to pin.
name: count-keeps-elidable-named-map-native
pattern: |
  ⟦
    𝐵-before,
    𝜏-new ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.new,
      𝜏1 ↦ 𝑒-object
    ⟧,
    𝜏-dup ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.dup
    ⟧,
    𝜏-init ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.invokespecial,
      𝜏2 ↦ 𝑒-object,
      𝜏3 ↦ "<init>",
      𝜏4 ↦ "()V",
      𝜏5 ↦ Φ.false
    ⟧,
    𝜏-map ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.invokeinterface,
      𝜏6 ↦ "java/util/stream/Stream",
      𝜏7 ↦ "map",
      𝜏8 ↦ "(Ljava/util/function/Function;)Ljava/util/stream/Stream;",
      𝜏9 ↦ Φ.true
    ⟧,
    𝐵-between,
    𝜏-count ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.invokeinterface,
      𝜏-cclass ↦ 𝑒-cclass,
      𝜏-cmethod ↦ "count",
      𝜏-csignature ↦ "()J",
      𝜏-ciface ↦ 𝑒-ciface
    ⟧,
    𝐵-after
  ⟧
result: |
  ⟦
    𝐵-before,
    𝜏-new ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.new,
      𝜏1 ↦ 𝑒-object
    ⟧,
    𝜏-dup ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.dup
    ⟧,
    𝜏-init ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.invokespecial,
      𝜏2 ↦ 𝑒-object,
      𝜏3 ↦ "<init>",
      𝜏4 ↦ "()V",
      𝜏5 ↦ Φ.false
    ⟧,
    𝜏-map ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.invokeinterface,
      𝜏6 ↦ "java/util/stream/Stream",
      𝜏7 ↦ "map",
      𝜏8 ↦ "(Ljava/util/function/Function;)Ljava/util/stream/Stream;",
      𝜏9 ↦ Φ.true,
      reverted ↦ Φ.true
    ⟧,
    𝐵-between,
    𝜏-count ↦ ⟦
      φ ↦ Φ.jeo.opcode.invokeinterface,
      𝜏-cclass ↦ 𝑒-cclass,
      𝜏-cmethod ↦ "count",
      𝜏-csignature ↦ "()J",
      𝜏-ciface ↦ 𝑒-ciface
    ⟧,
    𝐵-after
  ⟧
